  "equipment_type": "Commercial boiler controller",
  "applies_to": "Smith Cast Iron Boilers (Mestek) S28 Series boilers with a HeatNet control and the HeatNet BACnet bridge.",
  "summary": "The S28 Series list is the HeatNet BACnet bridge object set for Smith S28 cast iron boilers. The bridge exposes fixed objects: the BMS writes heat demand, the system setpoint (with a countdown failsafe timer), outdoor-reset settings, DHW setpoint and the clock, and reads plant temperatures, boilers on, modulation, stack temperature and per-boiler interlock, valve, alarm and sensor flags for up to 16 boilers.",
  "bacnet_transport": [],
  "firmware": "Bridge configuration 2.50+ for some points; HeatNet firmware 1.40+ for some points",
  "default_device_instance": null,
  "access_inferred": false,
  "notes": [
    "Per-boiler binary values are printed once as Boiler##_<name> with an instance formula and are listed here at the boiler 1 instance: 1000-series base + (n - 1) x 32, 2000/3000-series base + (n - 1) x 16. Boiler 1 is the master or stand-alone boiler.",
    "Per-boiler analog inputs are printed as ranges and listed here for boiler 1 only: Runtime AI 48-63, Cycles AI 64-79, SupplyTemp AI 80-95, ReturnTemp AI 96-111, DHWTemp AI 112-127, Modulation AI 128-143 (boiler n = boiler 1 instance + n - 1).",
    "Bridge configuration 2.50+ with HeatNet firmware 1.40+ is needed for AV 15, AI 112-145 and BV 3000-3011.",
    "Same HeatNet bridge object list as the Hydrotherm KNSX v2.52 sheet (hydrotherm/knsx-heatnet-bacnet-bridge), with these differences: no system DHWTemp (AI 16), an added StackTemp (AI 145, PVC firmware only), Boiler##_IRIAlarm described as \"Valve Alarm\", and firmware 1.40 instead of 3.48.",
    "The document describes Boiler##_OutsideSensorNA with the same text as HeaderSensorNA ('Header Sensor not available'); the name suggests the outside sensor.",
    "Weekday values run 1 (Monday) to 7 (Sunday)."
  ],
  "integration": {
    "summary": "Connect the BMS to the master (boiler 1) HeatNet control. Write BV 1 HeatDemand to call for heat and AV 2 Setpoint for the system setpoint, and keep reloading AV 1 SetpointTimer so the plant does not fall back to its local setpoint. Read header/supply/return temperatures, boilers on, modulation and the per-boiler alarm and failed flags.",
    "minimum_points": [
      {
        "ref": "BV 1",
        "name": "HeatDemand",
        "why": "Heat demand from the BMS (1 = heat)"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 2",
        "name": "Setpoint",
        "why": "System setpoint, 40-220 °F"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 1",
        "name": "SetpointTimer",
        "why": "Failsafe countdown; reload before it reaches 0"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 144",
        "name": "OperatingSetpoint",
        "why": "Active setpoint in use"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 3",
        "name": "HeaderTemp",
        "why": "Header / system temperature, °F"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 1",
        "name": "BoilersOn",
        "why": "Number of boilers running"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 2",
        "name": "Modulation",
        "why": "System target modulation, %"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BV 1005",
        "name": "Boiler##_Running",
        "why": "Boiler 1 firing (add 32 per boiler number)"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BV 1002",
        "name": "Boiler##_Alarm",
        "why": "Boiler 1 alarm (add 32 per boiler number)"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BV 1003",
        "name": "Boiler##_Failed",
        "why": "Boiler 1 failed (add 32 per boiler number)"
      }
    ],
    "enable": "BV 1 HeatDemand puts the boiler (plant) into heating mode when set to 1; 0 removes the demand. The setpoint the BMS writes is AV 2 Setpoint.",
    "heartbeat": "AV 1 SetpointTimer (0-65535 s) is a BMS failsafe countdown. The BMS must reload it periodically; if it reaches zero the control assumes the BMS has stopped and reloads its own saved local setpoint. Writing any read/write variable reloads the timer to 60 s if it is below 60 (on control firmware below 1.40 only writing the setpoint does this).",
    "remote_sensors": "AV 3-7 and BV 2 set up outdoor air reset; there is no writable outdoor temperature or flow value on this bridge.",
    "setup": [
      "The S28 object list does not state the transport (BACnet IP or BACnet MS/TP) or the bridge IP, MAC or baud defaults.",
      "To set the clock, write AV 8-14 (month, day, year, hour, minute, second, weekday) and then write 1 to BV 3 SetClock."
    ],
    "gotchas": [
      "If SetpointTimer runs out, the plant quietly returns to its local setpoint.",
      "Per-boiler objects are listed at the boiler 1 instance; offset them by boiler number using the formulas in the notes. Boiler 1 is the master or stand-alone boiler.",
      "Per-boiler modulation (AI 128-143) does not work in AA/High Fire, T1 or T2 modes."
    ]
  },
